        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Turquoise is a hydrated copper aluminium phosphate, sky blue to blue-green. A secondary mineral, it forms near the surface in arid to semi-arid climates, in the weathering zone of copper deposits or aluminium-rich volcanic rocks: rainwater dissolves copper from sulphides and phosphorus from apatite, then turquoise slowly precipitates in fissures and cavities as veins and nodules. The host matrix, brown or black limonite, sometimes forms a network called “spiderweb”. Iron turns it green.",
            "Triclinic system, in microcrystalline aggregates. Veins, nodules and crusts; visible crystals extremely rare (Virginia). No visible cleavage; conchoidal to granular fracture. Hardness 5 to 6; specific gravity 2.6 to 2.9; waxy to dull lustre; opaque; refractive index about 1.61 to 1.65. Porous: most turquoise on the market is resin-stabilised, waxed or treated (Zachery process), and many imitations exist (dyed howlite and magnesite, glass, synthetics). It is harmed by cosmetics, oils, perspiration, heat and detergents, which turn it green.",
            "Iran: Nishapur (Khorasan), the historic source of uniform sky-blue “Persian” turquoise, mined for over 2,000 years. Egypt: Sinai (Serabit el-Khadim, Wadi Maghara), the pharaohs' mines. United States: Arizona (Sleeping Beauty, Kingman, Bisbee), Nevada (Lander Blue, Number 8), New Mexico (Cerrillos) and Colorado, at the heart of Native American jewellery. China (Hubei, Shiyan), the main current production; Tibet, Mexico, Afghanistan. Its name comes from “Turkish stone”, as it reached Europe via Turkey.",
            "A stone of protection, wisdom and communication, one of humanity's oldest amulets, worn by the Aztecs, the Persians and the Navajo. It is credited with protecting travellers and bringing calm. It is associated with the throat chakra and the sign of Sagittarius, and is December's birthstone. Cleanse by smudging or a very brief rinse in lukewarm water, without soap; recharge in moonlight, never in the sun."
